SUMMARY:Walk on the Wild Side
DESCRIPTION:Join horticulture staff and experienced volunteers on a walk around the Blomquist Garden of Native Plants to learn about connections between people\, plants and place. Each month will feature a different seasonal topic related to gardening with native plants. \nFee: $10; free for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Parking fees apply.\n \nLocation: Meet at the gatehouse entrance to the Blomquist Garden of Native Plants (location 202 on the Gardens map).\n \nAccessibility: This is a small group program that takes place outdoors\, traveling on gravel paths with some uneven surfaces\, moderate inclines and stairs.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/walk-on-the-wild-side-11/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens – Gatehouse Entrance to Blomquist Garden of Native Plants\, 420 Anderson St.\, Durham\, 27708\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/Duke-Gardens-Blomquist-Prairie-by-Clarence-Burke.jpg
