SUMMARY:Finding Joy: Plant Meditation and Sculpture
DESCRIPTION:In this accessible workshop\, participants use sculpture and plant wisdom as pathways to self-discovery.  Led by sculptor and certified mindfulness instructor Meg Stein (CFP\, MFA)\, this workshop invites participants to engage in hands-on clay sculpting while practicing embodied meditation\, fostering deeper self-connection and artistic expression. The meditation will incorporate information and metaphorical wisdom from a plant in Duke Gardens. All skill levels are welcome. Participants are invited to attend just as they are; there is no need to know anything about mindfulness or sculpture (or plants!) in order to benefit from the exercises in this workshop. \nFee: $44; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Parking fees apply. \nLocation: Pelham-Cullen Classroom inside the Barnes Welcome Center. \nAccessibility: This program takes place partially seated indoors and partially outdoors\, traveling on a combination of paved and unpaved paths with some uneven surfaces and moderate inclines. The indoor location is equipped with a hearing loop\, which transmits sound directly to hearing aids and cochlear implants with a T-coil setting. Accessible restrooms are available onsite.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/finding-joy-plant-meditation-and-sculpture/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens–Pelham-Cullen Classroom in the Barnes Welcome Center\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27705\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/clay.jpg
END:VEVENT
