SUMMARY:Botanical Embroidery as Visible Mending
DESCRIPTION:In this two-hour class with Julia Gartrell\, artist and creator of the Radical Repair Workshop\, students will learn how to embroider botanical designs onto garments.  This is a great way to jazz up a shirt\, bag\, hat or any fabric that could use an embellishment.  These designs can also be used for visible mending\, covering up a small hole or stain that needs disguising.  While no sewing experience is needed\, a basic understanding of hand stitching will be helpful.  Supplies will be provided. \nFee: $38; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Parking fees apply. \nLocation: Pelham-Cullen Classroom inside the Barnes Welcome Center.\n \nAccessibility: This program takes place seated in an indoor location accessible via paved surfaces and equipped with a hearing loop\, which transmits sound directly to hearing aids and cochlear implants with a T-coil setting. Accessible restrooms are available onsite.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/botanical-embroidery-as-visible-mending/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens–Pelham-Cullen Classroom in the Barnes Welcome Center\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27705\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/Quilt-Julia-Gartrell-chenilledetail-220x220-embroidery.jpg
END:VEVENT
